          "id": "ff55b96f-736d-4f4f-bac4-b2e0d287b367",
          "name": "Custom field details",
          "request": {
            "name": "Custom field details",
            "description": {
              "content": "## Custom Field attributes\n* `handle` (string) - The key for a `contact` resource, e.g. `custom_1`, `custom_2`, `custom_3`\n* `title` (string) - The title of the custom field\n* `type` (string) - The type of the custom field\n* `required` (boolean) - Whether the custom field is required\n* `archived` (boolean) - Whether the custom field is archived\n## Sparse Fields\nUse the `fields[custom_fields]` parameter to include only specific attributes:\n### Include only handle and title fields\n* `GET /v1/custom_fields/123?fields[custom_fields]=handle,title`\n\nResponse will include only the specified fields\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"123\",\n    \"type\": \"custom_fields\",\n    \"attributes\": {\n      \"handle\": \"custom_1\",\n      \"title\": \"Favorite Song\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "custom_fields",
                ":id"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "fields[custom_fields]",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Partial attributes as specified, e.g. fields[custom_fields]=title,handle"
                }
              ],
              "variable": [
